=2 Walkthrough
* Talk to {n:Emhi Tchaoryo} to begin this Op.
* Exit to {z:West Sarutabaruta (S)} and hug the left wall to (I-9) to find the {n:Allied Ensign}. Once the party leader selects the "enter" option, you will be transported into {z:Ghoyu's Reverie}.
* At the start, two Student Salvemixers will pop. Speak to them to have them follow you, then proceed southwest to a room with 8 wounded solders.
* Speaking to the Salvemixers will show the following menu options:
** Give the physician orders.
*** Commence healing, stat!
*** Specify healing methods.
**** Prescribe what type of treatment?
***** Cures and physical healing.
***** Status ailment recovery.
*** Offer moral support.
*** Rest and recover.
*** Issue no orders.
* When you are close to a solder who is injured, use the "Commence healing, stat!" command to order the Salvemixer to use a single Cure spell. Multiple uses will be required.
** If a solder says "P-p-poisoned... C-c-can't b-b-breathe..." or "You must help me! I can't move my arms or legs!", use the "Prescribe what type of treatment?" option and chose "Status ailment recovery" to switch the Salvemixer to use the appropriate status spells.
*** After toggling the treatment type, order the Salvemaker to "Commence healing, stat!" to have them cast the status cure spell.
*** Since this is a toggle, be sure to use the "Prescribe what type of treatment?" option to change back to "Cures and physical healing" mode after the status ailment is cured.
** When a solder is sufficiently cured, his/her name will turn green and will say "I owe you my life. Many thanks!".
*** This happens below 100% health. The Salvemixers will not continue to heal a sufficiently healed NPC.
** If the Salvemixer runs out of MP, use the "rest and recover" option to restore MP before continuing.
*** They may also automatically begin resting with lines of dialogue indicating they are out of MP: "My magic does not run deep, I fear. I've reached my limit..."
** If the Salvemixer says "I'm not sure I'm cut out for this..." or "This is an uphill battle... I feel powerless...", use the "Offer moral support" option.
*** Using this option too often seems to annoy the Salvemixer.
*** They run literally all the way back to their start position and back to you even __after__ you've successfully offered moral support. Just wait for them to come back.
* When 6 out of the 8 injured solders are cured, you will get the message that the operation is complete.
** You can still heal the final soldiers for additional rewards if you like.
** Return to the Dawn Aureola to receive your XP and finish the Campaign Op.
** You will not receive XP if you are too far from the Dawn Aureola when the leader examines it.
* Return to {n:Emhi Tchaoryo} to complete this Op.

